  "lineage": "Belo Horizonte regional strain of Brazilian funk that emerged in Minas Gerais baile circuits from the mid-2010s, codified by DJ Win, MC Neguinho do Kaxeta's BH collaborators and the 'beat de BH' producers — running 130-150 BPM over a hard, dry tamborzão-derived kick-and-clap montagem, aggressive detuned lead stabs and sampled vocal snips looped into the beat, with MCs rapping in fast, percussive, heavily regional-accented delivery and a mix built for cheap PA horn stacks rather than club subwoofers.",
